"[{\"u\":\"/bpmn/\",\"len\":1852,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 ReferenceOn this pageBPMN 2.0 Reference LoyJoy is based on the BPMN 2.0 modeling standard and implements a BPMN 2.0 process engine. In the following all LoyJoy BPMN 2.0 modeling elements are described. Business Process Model And Notation (BPMN)​ Business Process Model And Notation (BPMN) is a standard for modeling business processes in form of flowchart diagrams. BPMN basically is a way to specify business processes with a standardized diagram representation, which e.g. in a simple form could be a vacation approval process. LoyJoy is based on BPMN and extends it using a standardized BPMN extension mechanism, ensuring that all LoyJoy agents are in fact standardized BPMN process models. The BPMN specification is maintained by the Object Management Group (OMG), which also with the Unified Modeling Language (UML) maintains one of the most important modeling languages in computer science. This goes so far that BPMN actually is specified with help of UML, applying UML as a meta-modeling language. BPMN Process Engine​ The goal of BPMN is to provide a process modeling language, that can be understood by business users, and at the same time is able to represent complex process semantics. By representing complex process semantics, it is possible to automatically execute BPMN process modules with a BPMN process engine. LoyJoy implements such a BPMN process engine. When you create a chat agent in LoyJoy Manager, you actually create a BPMN process model, which is extended with Lo\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\" approval process. LoyJoy is based on BPMN and extends it using a standardized BPMN extension mechanism, ensuring that all LoyJoy agents are in fact standardized BPMN process models. The BPMN specification is maintained by the Object Management Group (OMG), which also with the Unified Modeling Language (UML) maintains \",\"lly execute BPMN process modules with a BPMN process engine. LoyJoy implements such a BPMN process engine. When you create a chat agent in LoyJoy Manager, you actually create a BPMN process model, which is extended with LoyJoy-specific process module semantics. When you add a process module to your chat agent, effectiv\",\"a BPMN process model, which is extended with LoyJoy-specific process module semantics. When you add a process module to your chat agent, effectively you create a BPMN subprocess in the BPMN process model, and add LoyJoy-specific attributes to the subprocess. E.g. in case of the Email process module, you specify in this\"],\"nh\":3},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/control_flow/\",\"len\":42,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 Control FlowBPMN 2.0 Control Flow\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/control_flow/Loop/\",\"len\":458,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 Control FlowLoopOn this pageLoop To repeat a certain part of a process, you can use the loop. It can repeat several modules, several or the whole process. It is useful to provide the loop with a condition, otherwise it will be triggered every time. Here are some use cases: Loyalty Points​ Conditioning with the process variable \\\"loyaty_balance\\\" Participations​ Conditioning with the function \\\"Number of participations of the customer in all agents\\\"\",\"imgs\":[\"loop-7702a5ab6e98e79cf984fb50fe5d003f.png|Loop\",\"loyalty-6a78ffff6f438b9245b3b2c213b60ed1.png|Loyalty\",\"participations-36cff0ae754b23643eb27d5a5d12f171.png|participations\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"process variable \\\"loyaty_balance\\\" Participations​ Conditioning with the function \\\"Number of participations of the customer in all agents\\\"\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/\",\"len\":79,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsBPMN 2.0 Events Add BPMN start and BPMN end events to your flow.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/endEvent/\",\"len\":234,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsEnd EventEnd Event Insert this event to end the chat flow. Like the start event, an end event is predefined in each agent. However, it may be useful to indicate an end in other places (especially for multiple branches).\",\"imgs\":[\"StartEndEvent-7f13064b6f29431c21a181510b70605d.png|StartEndEvent\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"PMN 2.0 EventsEnd EventEnd Event Insert this event to end the chat flow. Like the start event, an end event is predefined in each agent. However, it may be useful to indicate an end in other places (especially for multiple branches).\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/intermediateCatchEvent_timer/\",\"len\":279,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsWait EventWait Event Use this if you want to have a waiting time before the next message appears in the chat window. Build a pause into the chat to build suspense, give the customer time to think, or give them time to complete a task (for example, baking recipes).\",\"imgs\":[\"intermediateCatchEvent_timer-067a985b7c982d420e019cdbdedd6bfe.png|Wait\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/startEvent_message/\",\"len\":712,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsMessage Start EventMessage Start Event The message start event is a type of start event that is triggered by the receipt of a message. It indicates that the process will begin when a user message entered in the footer is received. The message start event is typically followed by an AI Agent module that processes the user's message and generates a response. infoHaving a message start event in your process ensures that the chat footer (input area) is activated and visible to users, allowing them to type and send messages. infoThe message start event should be preceded by an end event so the rest of the process flow does not 'leak' into the message handling following the message start event.\",\"imgs\":[\"icon-3fbd025d1bc97f795bb79c1843123196.png|Start\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"the process will begin when a user message entered in the footer is received. The message start event is typically followed by an AI Agent module that processes the user's message and generates a response. infoHaving a message start event in your process ensures that the chat footer (input area) is activated and visibl\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/startEvent_timer/\",\"len\":1317,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsTimer eventOn this pageTimer event Start your chat history on a day of your choice and adjust the time zone if necessary. Simply drag the timer event to the beginning of the flow and decide whether it should be executed once or several times. The timer event can be used if the chat should restart automatically on a regular basis (e.g. daily in the Advent calendar). The chat will then restart automatically every day at the timer event, and can e.g. lead to different chat branches for day-specific content. Typical Use Cases​ Top use case is an advent calendar but there are many possible applications like live shows How to Use the Module​ To test the function, you select a day from the drop-down list and restart it: Advent Calendar​ In the specific case of the Advent calendar, set the timer next to the start event so that the entry can be both. The settings of the start timer are as follows: The Advent calendar begins anew every day so that the next door can be opened. Useful Tips​ A similar behavior can be created by setting the chat to storage duration \\\"0 minutes\\\", i.e. having the chat restart every time the page is loaded. However, unlike the timer event, this will not restart the chat on a timed basis if the customer does not reload the web page with the chat, i.e. leaves it open.\",\"imgs\":[\"IuAhQMJ4gNBKBEIIkDAhdOhHBDwESBgPEFqJQAgBEiaEDv2IgIcACeMBQisRCCHwHxA2gEzT635CAAAAAElFTkSuQmCC|icon\",\"setting-8c488ec1eeda70a148734dca0f9aa69f.png|setting\",\"TimerPreview-edd00d8bd13c76a4d457621156da1816.gif|TimerPreview\",\"advCalStart-d615ee840c7db2cfbb3d726efea79697.png|advCalStart\",\"advCalSetting-a3589e410e89f1edd38b3a4f867c8921.png|advCalSetting\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/events/startEvent/\",\"len\":136,\"t\":\"BPMN 2.0 EventsStart eventStart event The start event is the first event in a process. It indicates the beginning of a process instance.\",\"imgs\":[\"icon-97c6ae08c2bea0efda9f80e1dec81f98.png|Start\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/\",\"len\":1131,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesOn this pageBPMN Process Modules LoyJoy ships more than 110 BPMN process modules that you drag and drop into the Process Editor. Each module encapsulates predefined logic, from \\\"ask for first name\\\" to \\\"AI Agent with tool calling\\\". Clusters​ AI: AI Agent for tool calling, knowledge, web search, MCP Service: Live Chat, Handover via Email, Appointment Scheduler Sales / Commerce: Product Feed, Product Gallery, Coupon Code, Loyalty Points Auth / Compliance: Auth0, Keycloak, Microsoft Entra ID, OneTrust, Personal Data Intro CRM / Marketing: Salesforce Service Cloud, Hubspot, Mailchimp, Brevo Integrations: API Client, Web Service, Zapier, Workato Add process modules to your chat flow​ Simply drag and drop the module onto the process editor canvas, below the black circle which marks the start event. Remove process modules from your chat flow​ Again drag the module and move it over to the left where you find the process modules (we call it the process module palette). Drop the module when \\\"Drop to delete\\\" appears. This action cannot be reversed. The following list of BPMN process modules is constantly evolving.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\" modules that you drag and drop into the Process Editor. Each module encapsulates predefined logic, from \\\"ask for first name\\\" to \\\"AI Agent with tool calling\\\". Clusters​ AI: AI Agent for tool calling, knowledge, web search, MCP Service: Live Chat, Handover via Email, Appointment Scheduler Sales / Commerce: Product Feed,\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/advent_calendar_door/\",\"len\":260,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAdvent Calendar Door ModuleAdvent Calendar Door Module Let customers open a new door every day in a Christmas advent calendar countdown. To learn how to set a timer click here. infoOutside the advent period, the chat session will end automatically.\",\"imgs\":[\"advent_calendar_door_demo-bd9ddbd3e582d2990302483691cee1dc.png|advent_calendar_door_demo\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_agent/\",\"len\":19948,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI AgentOn this pageAI Agent Overview​ The AI Agent module is LoyJoy's new component for building AI-driven conversational experiences. It allows an AI to understand user intent and use a set of tools to respond to requests and complete tasks. The agent can operate iteratively, meaning it can call multiple tools in sequence (e.g., search a knowledge base, then read a full document, then search the web) before formulating a final answer for the user. This module replaces the older AI Gateway, AI Knowledge, AI Prompt, AI Smalltalk and AI Recommender modules. It combines the functionality of all those modules into a single, more capable module. If your existing chats use the old modules, we recommend migrating them to the new AI Agent module. Key Concepts​ The AI Agent module is built on two core components: Instructions (Prompts): This is where you define the AI's rules and persona. You configure its behavior and provide it with the necessary context to do its job. Tools: These are the actions the AI agent can perform. You give the agent a set of capabilities (like searching knowledge or running a process), and it will intelligently decide which one to use—or which combination of tools to use—based on the user's query. How to Set Up Your AI Agent​ Configuring your agent is a step-by-step process. 1. Add the Module​ Start by adding the \\\"AI Agent\\\" module to your process. This single module will handle the conversational experience. 2. Select an AI Model​ Choose the un\",\"imgs\":[\"question_count-0e45f844491184ea192ab9054a9e37e7.png|question_count\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesAI AgentOn this pageAI Agent Overview​ The AI Agent module is LoyJoy's new component for building AI-driven conversational experiences. It allows an AI to understand user intent and use a set of tools to respond t\",\"BPMN ModulesAI AgentOn this pageAI Agent Overview​ The AI Agent module is LoyJoy's new component for building AI-driven conversational experiences. It allows an AI to understand user intent and use a set of tools to respond to requests and complete tasks. The agent can operate iteratively, meaning i\",\"onal experiences. It allows an AI to understand user intent and use a set of tools to respond to requests and complete tasks. The agent can operate iteratively, meaning it can call multiple tools in sequence (e.g., search a knowledge base, then read a full document, then search the web) before formulating a final answe\"],\"nh\":96},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_knowledge_followup/\",\"len\":1026,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI FollowupOn this pageAI Followup This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ AI Knowledge is a module that allows you to answer your customer’s questions using AI. However, to create a decent context to answer the question, the question needs to be atomic, hence not referencing any previous questions. Consider the following dialog between a human and an AI assistant: Human: What is the weather like today? AI: It is sunny. Human: What about tomorrow? To answer the second question, the AI needs to know that the second question is a follow-up question to the first question. This is not possible with the AI Knowledge module. The AI Knowledge Followup module allows you to create a standalone follow-up question that can be answered with AI Knowledge. The question of the user will be rephrased such that it contains enough context to be answered by AI Knowledge. The rephrased question the module will provide would be: Human: What will the weather be like tomorrow?\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesAI FollowupOn this pageAI Followup This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ AI Knowledge is a module that allows you to answer your customer’s questions using AI. However, to create a decent context to answer the question, the \",\"use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ AI Knowledge is a module that allows you to answer your customer’s questions using AI. However, to create a decent context to answer the question, the question needs to be atomic, hence not referencing any previous questions. Consider the following dialog between a human a\",\"e question needs to be atomic, hence not referencing any previous questions. Consider the following dialog between a human and an AI assistant: Human: What is the weather like today? AI: It is sunny. Human: What about tomorrow? To answer the second question, the AI needs to know that the second question is a follow-up \"],\"nh\":7},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_knowledge/\",\"len\":9585,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI KnowledgeOn this pageAI Knowledge This module is not deprecated, however limited to answering customer questions based on a static knowledge database, which is queried once per question. This implements the classical Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) approach. For new use cases, please consider using the newer AI Agent module instead, which is more powerful due to its ability to call the knowledge database multiple times per question, and to call additional tools such as web search, product search, and more. This is necessary for more complex use cases and possible sinnce middle of 2025 with the advent of agentic AI / AI agents. Introduction​ Answer your customer’s questions using Large Langague Models. The LLM will consider the sources you provide via Knowledge. Optionally, you can integrate an external Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline with Microsoft Azure AI Search (e.g. to connect Sharepoint). You can also connect sources via Model Context Protocol (MCP), add a web search, and the content of the current web page the user is on. So in contrast to the AI Smalltalk module, the AI Knowlede module is based on the knowledge base. Prerequisites​ Add sources or catalogs to Knowledge​ The AI Knowledge module can use the sources and catalogs that you have stored under Knowledge. The content of your added sources are used by the AI Knowledge module to answer customer questions. Add AI Knowledge to your Agent​ If your agent has not activated the use of A\",\"imgs\":[\"flow-d72616acefe1b01a75a5ea0d85282b2e.png|flow\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\". This implements the classical Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) approach. For new use cases, please consider using the newer AI Agent module instead, which is more powerful due to its ability to call the knowledge database multiple times per question, and to call additional tools such as web search, product search\",\"duct search, and more. This is necessary for more complex use cases and possible sinnce middle of 2025 with the advent of agentic AI / AI agents. Introduction​ Answer your customer’s questions using Large Langague Models. The LLM will consider the sources you provide via Knowledge. Optionally, you can integrate an exte\",\"f 2025 with the advent of agentic AI / AI agents. Introduction​ Answer your customer’s questions using Large Langague Models. The LLM will consider the sources you provide via Knowledge. Optionally, you can integrate an external Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline with Microsoft Azure AI Search (e.g. to conne\"],\"nh\":42},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_prompt/\",\"len\":1602,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI PromptOn this pageAI Prompt This module is supposed to be used inside the normal chat flow. It is used to generate a response based on a predefined system message and predefined user message, i.e. not necessarily a user message. Inside the system message and user message you can use LoyJoy variables as well as expressions. The response is generated by the AI model based on the system message and user message. The output is stored in a variable of your choice or returned as the bot message. The prompt can be adapted to your needs by prompting techniques. Use Cases​ The AI prompt module is very flexible can be used in various use cases. Here are some examples: Generate a JSON string to query an API based on user input Generate a SQL query based on user input Use the AI model to make a decision based on user input Response format​ Normally, AI models generate text responses. However, you can also force the AI model to produce a JSON response. This is helpful if you want to extract structured information from the model response. To do this, you need to create mappings for the attributes you are interested in. Imagine you prompt AI to read an email to extract the sender and the subject. The prompt could look like this: Dear Ladies and Gentlemen,I am writing to you to inform you about the new product we have launched....Cheers,Sandra Smith To extract the relevant information you are interested in, create a mapping like this: The name of the sender is then available i\",\"imgs\":[\"ai_prompt_json_mapping-dadf7e7699921f498fc4e55d3ec28e4b.png|AI Prompt module mapping configuration showing a target variable, source field, and description for extracting the sender name from an email.\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\" Inside the system message and user message you can use LoyJoy variables as well as expressions. The response is generated by the AI model based on the system message and user message. The output is stored in a variable of your choice or returned as the bot message. The prompt can be adapted to your needs by prompting \",\"le of your choice or returned as the bot message. The prompt can be adapted to your needs by prompting techniques. Use Cases​ The AI prompt module is very flexible can be used in various use cases. Here are some examples: Generate a JSON string to query an API based on user input Generate a SQL query based on user inpu\",\"re are some examples: Generate a JSON string to query an API based on user input Generate a SQL query based on user input Use the AI model to make a decision based on user input Response format​ Normally, AI models generate text responses. However, you can also force the AI model to produce a JSON response. This is hel\"],\"nh\":6},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_recommender/\",\"len\":635,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI RecommenderOn this pageAI Recommender This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module takes a user message and generates an appropriate product recommendation based on it. To make this recommendation, it searches the product database using SQL queries. The module is designed to be used after the message start event, not inside the chat flow. To improve the quality of the recommendations, you can add information to the system message on how to interpret the user message and how to generate the SQL query. For this module to work, you need to have a product database.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesAI RecommenderOn this pageAI Recommender This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module takes a user message and generates an appropriate prod\",\"BPMN ModulesAI RecommenderOn this pageAI Recommender This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module takes a user message and generates an appropriate product recommendation based on it. To make this recommendation, it searches the product \",\" Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module takes a user message and generates an appropriate product recommendation based on it. To make this recommendation, it searches the product database using SQL queries. The module is designed to be used after the message start event, not inside the c\"],\"nh\":4},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/ai_smalltalk/\",\"len\":420,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAI SmalltalkOn this pageAI Smalltalk This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module aims to respond to small talk requests. In contrast to the AI Knowledge module, the AI Smalltalk module is not based on a knowledge base. Instead, it generates responses based on the prompt and the system message, which can be adapted to your needs by prompting techniques.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesAI SmalltalkOn this pageAI Smalltalk This module is deprecated. Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module aims to respond to small talk requests. In contrast to the AI Knowledge module, the AI Smalltalk module is not based on a knowledge base. I\",\"Please only use the AI Agent module instead. Introduction​ This module aims to respond to small talk requests. In contrast to the AI Knowledge module, the AI Smalltalk module is not based on a knowledge base. Instead, it generates responses based on the prompt and the system message, which can be adapted to your needs \"],\"nh\":2},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/animation/\",\"len\":2098,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAnimation ModuleOn this pageAnimation Module Introduction​ Animations will lighten up any agent and are a real joy factor of the LoyJoy Platform. They are played as background animation within the chat UI (User Interface). There are several great animations included into LoyJoy you can choose from! This article covers the many different ways you can use them to wow your customers. Typical Use Cases​ For example, you can use animations for raffles, events including holidays, or other occasions. Within a raffle, you can include different animations depending on how the customer chooses to answer a question. They are also a lot of fun to use for your festive agents such as advent calendars, easter bots or sporting events. In short, the purposeful use of gamification elements like animations can enhance any agent. We have Animations from the following categories: Easter Hopping bunny Tripping bunny Easter eggs Christmas Santa jumping Christmas balls Candy cane Christmas trees Gingerbread man Christmas stocking Seasons Autumn leaves Snowflakes at night Snowflakes by day Pumpkins Pine cones Other Balloons Happy unicorn Confetti Cheese Firework at night Firework by day Soccer ball Gift boxes Gold glitter Balloon letters LogoSlam Lotto Magenta confetti Magenta snowflakes Poo Balloons golden stars Balloons red hearts Balloons colorful hearts Balloons colourful stars Balloons blue stars Balloons NIVEA Balloons magenta Raining stars Golden raining stars And many more! How to\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesAnimation ModuleOn this pageAnimation Module Introduction​ Animations will lighten up any agent and are a real joy factor of the LoyJoy Platform. They are played as background animation within the chat UI (User Interface). There are several great animations included into LoyJoy y\",\"fferent animations depending on how the customer chooses to answer a question. They are also a lot of fun to use for your festive agents such as advent calendars, easter bots or sporting events. In short, the purposeful use of gamification elements like animations can enhance any agent. We have Animations from the foll\",\" calendars, easter bots or sporting events. In short, the purposeful use of gamification elements like animations can enhance any agent. We have Animations from the following categories: Easter Hopping bunny Tripping bunny Easter eggs Christmas Santa jumping Christmas balls Candy cane Christmas trees Gingerbread man Ch\"],\"nh\":6},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/api_client/\",\"len\":9569,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAPI ClientOn this pageAPI Client Introduction​ Make use of the API client module whenever you want to send collected data from LoyJoy to your service, pull data from your service to LoyJoy, or you simply want to trigger external services. The API requests configured in this module are executed by a LoyJoy server, not the user’s browser. Typical Use Cases / Examples​ Typical use cases are exporting data from LoyJoy to your web service or reading data from external resources. Reading data from an external service​ As an example, we want to read the current price of a product to be shown in the chat flow. To do this, we set the method to GET and enter the URL with the ID of the product, for example http://example.org/getPrice?product-id=123abc. We could also use a dynamic product ID, for example stored in the LoyJoy variable product_id. Then the URL would be http://example.org/getPrice?product-id=${product_id}. Let's assume this request will generate a JSON response body of this form: { \\\"price\\\": { \\\"amount\\\": 125, \\\"currency\\\": \\\"Euro\\\", \\\"validUntil\\\": \\\"2022-12-31\\\" }, \\\"productId\\\": \\\"123abc\\\"} We can then map the field /price/amount of the JSON response body to a variable of our liking, for example product_price: By going through this process module, the GET request will be executed and the product_price variable will be filled with the value from the request. Afterwards, the product_price variable can be used in any text field. Sending data to an external service​ This can be\",\"imgs\":[\"api_client1-44fa839cbec68716d268b9b0d9df3082.png|grafik\",\"api_client2-9a00fdacc665615a9baff7bd8b8aa9eb.png|grafik\",\"image1-46924eb18ac57106afede60ce8051cf9.png|Image1\",\"overview-45ac234b91ccdbc8170816742ba49254.png|Api client overview\",\"image2-c0e0a0ba710fb58641d0d0bed06782fd.png|Image2\",\"api_client_log_debug-7266a8dd61ec4fbc1154533a7e8e6e3e.png|Log debug\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/api_client/mappings/\",\"len\":4472,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAPI ClientMappingsOn this pageMappings Mappings allow either to send data such as process variables from LoyJoy to an external API, or to extract data from an external API and write it into LoyJoy process variables. Send Data from LoyJoy to External API​ When process modules such as the CleverReach module send data, the API usually expects data in JSON format. To send information to the API, you can use mappings. LoyJoy follows the JSON pointer standard to send information to the API. Mapping to JSON property based on Target JSON Pointer​ In the following example a LoyJoy process variable firstname is written to JSON with the key first_name. Please note, that the key first_name is denoted by the JSON pointer /first_name, i.e. the leading slash / is required by the JSON pointer standard. { \\\"first_name\\\": \\\"John\\\"} Mapping to JSON object based on Target JSON Pointer​ In the following example a LoyJoy process variable street is written into the JSON object store_address with the key street. { \\\"store_address\\\": { \\\"street\\\": \\\"Main Street 20\\\" }} Mapping to JSON array based on Target JSON Pointer​ In the following example a LoyJoy process variable street is written the first element of the JSON array addresses at position 0, with the key street. { \\\"addresses\\\": [ { \\\"street\\\": \\\"Main Street 20\\\" } ]} Retrieve Data from External API into LoyJoy​ When process modules such as the API client module retrieve data from an API, the data is usually in JSON or XML format. To extract inform\",\"imgs\":[\"image1-9c96369f71493361b94fc8bd34a0de03.png|Image1\",\"image2-2765ba48918e60f96ab96354c4583a75.png|Image2\",\"image3-f938b992d69902d556899609426344c5.png|Image3\",\"image11-6aed0a839795a38306863fdfd3eb685d.png|Image11\",\"image12-3457a097cab15143129385ae885a8eb8.png|Image12\",\"image13-8dd6e0e82fc6a6682f201d48a68d8238.png|Image13\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/api_client/timeouts/\",\"len\":2453,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAPI ClientTimeoutsOn this pageTimeouts Process modules with API calls such as the API client process module and the Webservice process module have a timeout of approximately 20 seconds. This means that the process module will wait for a response from the server for approximately 20 seconds. If the server does not respond within this time, the process module will classify this as a timeout, log it in the runtime log, and continue with the next process module. So if such timeouts occur in the runtime log of your tenant, please check with the developer of your API if the server is reachable and responds in time. Can LoyJoy extend the timeout duration of 20 seconds?​ Unfortunately, we cannot extend the timeout duration of 20 seconds. This is because the process module is executed in the context of a chat. If we would extend the timeout duration, the chat would be blocked for this time, showing a typing indicator. This would be a bad user agent and heavily influence conversion rates. Also, please take into consideration that one chat message could trigger multiple process modules with API calls, which would sum up. For the worst case the LoyJoy chat UI itself has a timeout of approximately 30 seconds, and then will resend the chat for multiple times, inducing a loop. But I need more than 20 seconds to process the request in my server!​ If you cannot optimize your server response time, you can enable \\\"Use request queue?\\\" in the process module configuration. This will qu\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\" would extend the timeout duration, the chat would be blocked for this time, showing a typing indicator. This would be a bad user agent and heavily influence conversion rates. Also, please take into consideration that one chat message could trigger multiple process modules with API calls, which would sum up. For the wo\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/appointment/\",\"len\":2831,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAppointment Scheduler ModuleOn this pageAppointment Scheduler Module Introduction​ The Appointment Scheduler Module is convenient to allow customers to book appointments directly in the chat. You can offer fixed timeslots from which customers can select their favorite time with a single click. Typical Use Cases​ The Appointment Scheduler Module offers a fast and uncomplicated way to book appointments. By setting timeslots in advance, you eliminate the tedious correspondence process of looking for suitable appointments. It is especially useful for service requests and arranging meetings. warningIf users do not find a suitable appointment slot, they might skip the module. If you use any process modules after the appointment module, be sure to condition them with empty appointment_at == false or similar. Otherwise they will be run even if no appointment was made. How to Use the Module​ Enter time slot. Design appointment invitation. Email notification​ You are able to automatically have an email sent as a notification to your own email address (not your customer's). Email content​ You can use any variables in the PDF and HTML template by using the correct notation ${...}. If you don't have an HTML email template, you can just start typing the text. If you use plain text, then it will not be formatted in any way. Time slots​ Time slots define, when appointments can be made. You have to add time slots for the process module to work properly. When a time slot is booked,\",\"imgs\":[\"appointment_demo-c2b128eb741418c73cb3d66b763842f3.png|appointment_demo\",\"appointment_scheduler_add_empty-673c0cd72df1af4ce39fab836de3ed51.png|appointment_scheduler_add_empty\",\"appointment_scheduler_add_timeslot-5caabe929410dac05d6c980a9d0efa1a.png|appointment_scheduler_add_timeslot\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/articles/\",\"len\":1158,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesArticle Gallery ModuleOn this pageArticle Gallery Module Introduction​ The Article Gallery module allows you to showcase up to 5 articles within the chat, displayed in a list format. When a user clicks on an article, a detailed view with all the relevant information about the article is presented. Typical Use Cases​ This module is ideal for displaying a small collection of products, featured items, or any set of articles you want users to explore directly within the chat interface. How to Use the Module​ Adding Articles​ Use the dropdown menu to select up to 5 articles you want to display. The articles available in the dropdown are managed in the Knowledge section, where you can create and maintain catalogs of products or articles. You can check out here on how to add new articles. Display in Chat​ Once set up, the articles will be displayed in a list format within the chat. Here's how it will look: Detailed View​ When a user clicks on an article from the list, they will see a detailed view with all the information you have provided about the article. This can include images, descriptions, prices, and any other relevant details.\",\"imgs\":[\"article_gallery_chat-25849566d2ca3add1a481d5e2019d0ea.png|article_gallery_chat\",\"article_gallery_detailed-9f86996549449c17ed09373f5976a884.png|article_gallery_detailed\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/audio_recorder/\",\"len\":914,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesVoice Recorder ModuleOn this pageVoice Recorder Module Introduction​ Unlike the Audio module, where audio files can be played, Audio Recording gives customers the option to leave a voice message in the chat. Typical Use Cases​ Can be used for service requests when describing the issue via chat would take too long. By means of a voice message, the situation can be described in more detail if necessary. How to Use the Module​ The following screenshot shows the module in action. Users are prompted to leave a voice message. Afterwards, the chat confirms that the voice message has been received. Useful Tips​ Sign in​ If the client is authenticated via the login module, you can access it as seen below ( Location). Either way, the audio message can be downloaded via the LoyJoy API. Location​ You can find the audio message under the customers menue. Click on the customer and go to the history tab.\",\"imgs\":[\"audio_recorder_demo-48a5d4e959841e9c2a1e5102c7e77fa6.png|audio_recorder_demo\",\"audio_recorder_customers-d1e1d4a071dae7d1bd1737609a25a31d.png|audio_recorder_customers\",\"audio_recorder_history-453f0155a11a6eb733690aa28720e8be.png|audio_recorder_history\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/audio/\",\"len\":1080,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesVoice Message ModuleOn this pageVoice Message Module Introduction​ Who doesn't love audio? Lighten up your chat agent by adding media in the form of audio. Add up to five voice messages or music files to your chat. Typical Use Cases​ Possible applications can be service requests as well as raffles. For example, audio clips can serve as the basis for quiz questions or provide detailed information in a more engaging manner. How to Use the Module​ Add file​ To add an audio file, you need to click on upload audio and upload your audio file. Display in Chat​ All uploaded voice messages will be displayed in the chat for users to play. Ensure your audio files are clear and concise for the best user agent. Useful Tips​ If you want to add more than five audio files to your chat, simply insert another Voice Message module into your agent. Be mindful that not all users may be able to play sound on their devices. Some users may agent sound restrictions or could be playing other music/sounds simultaneously, which will be interrupted when they play your audio clips.\",\"imgs\":[\"audio_demo-1c076d1e9915d3c63cdcaa0c45896e88.png|audio_demo\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesVoice Message ModuleOn this pageVoice Message Module Introduction​ Who doesn't love audio? Lighten up your chat agent by adding media in the form of audio. Add up to five voice messages or music files to your chat. Typical Use Cases​ Possible applications can be service requests as well as raffles. Fo\",\"d voice messages will be displayed in the chat for users to play. Ensure your audio files are clear and concise for the best user agent. Useful Tips​ If you want to add more than five audio files to your chat, simply insert another Voice Message module into your agent. Be mindful that not all users may be able to play \",\"nt. Useful Tips​ If you want to add more than five audio files to your chat, simply insert another Voice Message module into your agent. Be mindful that not all users may be able to play sound on their devices. Some users may agent sound restrictions or could be playing other music/sounds simultaneously, which will be \"],\"nh\":4},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/auth0/\",\"len\":1599,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesAuth0 ModuleOn this pageAuth0 Module This module allows customers to authenticate in the chat using an Auth0 user account based on OAuth 2.0. Simply provide the credentials from Auth0 to identify your customers within the chat. This enables seamless user identification and interaction within the chat. Typical Use Cases​ Use this module to authenticate users securely in the chat through Auth0, retrieve user information, and customize user agents based on their profile data. How to Use the Module​ Configure Redirect URIs: Set up the following redirect URIs in your Auth0 application settings: https://app-stable.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback https://app-runtime.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback https://runtime.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback These URIs are essential to guide users back to the chat post-authentication while maintaining security. Enter Auth0 Credentials: In the LoyJoy module, input your: Auth0 Domain Client ID Client Secret Scope These credentials will authenticate users and allow you to manage user sessions. Customize Texts: Adjust the text for the sign-in button and login prompts under \\\"Other Texts\\\" in the LoyJoy platform to match your branding. Mappings​ Configure source fields in mappings to retrieve user profile information. Default fields provided by Auth0 include: birthdate, family_name, email, email_verified, gender, given_name, locale, middle_name, name, nickname, phone_number, phone_number_verified, picture, preferred_username, profile, sub, w\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"se Cases​ Use this module to authenticate users securely in the chat through Auth0, retrieve user information, and customize user agents based on their profile data. How to Use the Module​ Configure Redirect URIs: Set up the following redirect URIs in your Auth0 application settings: https://app-stable.loyjoy.com/auth/\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/beiersdorf/\",\"len\":90,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesBeiersdorf ModuleBeiersdorf Module Integrate Beiersdorf API into your process.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/big_query/\",\"len\":4262,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesBigQuery ModuleOn this pageBigQuery Module Google BigQuery is a cloud-based big data analytics web service for processing very large read-only data sets. BigQuery was designed for analyzing data on the order of billions of rows, using a SQL-like syntax. With this process module you can save data in Google BigQuery in real-time for further processing and analysis. This allows you to build complex dashboards and data pipelines from your agent data. How to Use the Module​ Step 1: Create a dataset in BigQuery​ In your Google Cloud project, start by creating a new dataset in BigQuery. Provide a name for the dataset such as loyjoy_dataset and click \\\"Create dataset\\\". Step 2: Create a table inside your dataset​ In the list, click on your newly created dataset and create a new table by using the button that says \\\"Create table\\\". Provide a name for the table such as customers or variables. Next, you have to define a schema for your table. The schema defines the structure of your table, i.e. what kind of data you want to store in your table. If your want to store customer data, the schema could look like this: If you want to store arbitrary variables, the schema could look like this: Finally click \\\"Create table\\\". Step 3: Check the schema of your table​ In the list, click on your newly created table. For the customers table, the schema could look like this: For the variables table, the schema could look like this: Step 4: Create a service account​ In Google Cloud Platform open\",\"imgs\":[\"create_dataset-c3b919d5082a10d1abd76e416641e5fe.png|Create Dataset\",\"create_customers-79542803b403b9db1ea1ea72b0879952.png|Create Customers\",\"create_variables-628cd59039f4da8ac8ebfc446e8c5ac0.png|Create Variables\",\"schema_customers-90a808e20d0909d4f5dac65004d59a4f.png|Customers Schema\",\"schema_variables-b6ecb77ba44d143851148c38e0f2231f.png|Variables Schema\",\"service_account_step_1-8f4c6577c9e25375f1792c6b1a807ffb.png|Service Account Step 1\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"gQuery in real-time for further processing and analysis. This allows you to build complex dashboards and data pipelines from your agent data. How to Use the Module​ Step 1: Create a dataset in BigQuery​ In your Google Cloud project, start by creating a new dataset in BigQuery. Provide a name for the dataset such as loy\",\"be opened with any text editor. You will need the contents of this file in the next step. Step 5: Add the BigQuery Module to your Agent​ Either add the BigQuery module to your LoyJoy agent or use one of the templates from the LoyJoy Template Store. In the LoyJoy Template Store, you can find templates for saving custome\",\" of those templates to your tenant. Step 6: Configure the BigQuery Module​ The BigQuery module needs to know which data from your agent should be saved in BigQuery. This is done by defining field mappings. In case of the customers table, the field mappings would map the email, first name and last name to the correspond\"],\"nh\":5},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/birthdate/\",\"len\":928,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesBirthdate ModuleOn this pageBirthdate Module Introduction​ Ask for your customer's birthday and save this date if necessary. Typical Use Cases​ When a newsletter registration takes place in the chat, this can be used to save the date to congratulate on the birthday by newsletter. Furthermore helpful for promotions, as well as when a minimum age is required. How to Use the Module​ Minimum age​ By adding a minimum age the drop-down menu with the birth years will start when this age is reached. This feature is optional. Other texts​ Here you can add different intros/reactions/placeholders. Sign in​ If the customer is authenticated via the login, you can find his date of birth as shown below (location). It will be saved as a variable in any case, so you can export it via csv. Location​ Authenticated customers date of birth are shown under the customers menue. Click on the customer and go to the history tab.\",\"imgs\":[\"birthday_demo-9688980920ec06abd131c181d2f35328.png|birthday_demo\",\"birthday_history-210d743698e596e205751a49c83f0003.png|birthday_history\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/brevo/\",\"len\":1636,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesBrevo ModuleOn this pageBrevo Module Brevo is an application designed to help you manage and optimize your email marketing campaigns. For more information on Brevo, visit Brevo. This module allows you to insert subscriptions directly into Brevo, ensuring that your email marketing lists are always up-to-date. Also you can read contact data from Brevo. Typical Use Cases​ Adding a new contact to your email marketing list. Adding a new contact to your email marketing list with double opt-in flow. Read contact data such as the first name. How to Use the Module​ Email Input: Ensure you have the user's email address by using an Email module or Sign-in module earlier in your chat process. Api Key: Generate an api key in Brevo. List ID: Optionally, obtain your email list ID from Brevo. Configure the Module: Once you have the email address, Api Key and list ID, insert them into the module configuration in LoyJoy. Mappings​ You can define mappings to pass additional data from the chat to Brevo. By default only the email address is added to the contact. If you want to add additional information to the contact you can use mappings in the process module. This will add custom fields to the contact, such as: attributes.FIRSTNAME, attributes.LASTNAME, attributes.VORNAME, attributes.NACHNAME These fields are documented in the Brevo attributes documentation. The attributes can be configured freely as decribed in the Brevo API documentation. Please note that depending on the initial \",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0}]"